                <pb facs="0300" n="192" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg192"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No. 10—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Sacasa to Señores Barrios, Aguilar, and
                        Saballos.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-05-29"><hi rendition="#italic">May 29,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>With the important object of responding to the honorable mediation of his
                    excellency, the American minister, Mr. Lewis Baker, in order that our
                    disgraceful civil war may cease, you have been appointed by my Government to
                    immediately go to Sabana Grande to attend the conferences for the settlement of
                    peace, acting in accordance to the instructions which I inclose you
                    herewith.</p>
                <p>With the greatest consideration, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Roberto Sacasa.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
